{"uid":"920c572660c0b54d","name":"TestAppsSuite/TestContainerdCPUs","fullName":"github.com/lf-edge/eve/evetest/tests/apps.TestAppsSuite/TestContainerdCPUs","time":{"start":1795473273000,"stop":1795473525650,"duration":252650},"status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[],"testStage":{"steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},"afterStages":[],"labels":[{"name":"resultFormat","value":"junit"},{"name":"suite","value":"github.com/lf-edge/eve/evetest/tests/apps"},{"name":"testClass","value":"github.com/lf-edge/eve/evetest/tests/apps"},{"name":"package","value":"github.com/lf-edge/eve/evetest/tests/apps"}],"parameters":[],"links":[],"hidden":false,"retry":false,"extra":{"severity":"normal","retries":[],"categories":[],"history":{"statistic":{"failed":1,"broken":0,"skipped":0,"passed":24,"unknown":0,"total":25},"items":[{"uid":"5d9e1ade6abb1806","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/41/#testresult/5d9e1ade6abb1806","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795387642000,"stop":1795387897650,"duration":255650}},{"uid":"bfc99b2457a38829","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/36/#testresult/bfc99b2457a38829","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795301179000,"stop":1795301431130,"duration":252130}},{"uid":"b1a1979170b0f804","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/31/#testresult/b1a1979170b0f804","status":"failed","statusDetails":"Failed to setup devices [edge-dev]: rpc error: code = Unknown desc = failed to setup SDN device: device \"sdn-4bf7e75d\" already exists\n\nClaude's conclusion:\nThis fully confirms live evidence is consistent with the pattern seen in every prior failure tonight.\n\n**Root cause:** This is the same unresolved issue already diagnosed 12 times earlier in this run (`live-investigation.md`, starting with `TestCPUPlacementWholeCoreSMT`): at 23:11:40 the broker's teardown of SDN device `sdn-4bf7e75d` (Proxmox VM 111) timed out (`failed waiting for VM 111 deletion: context deadline exceeded`), but the broker wiped its local image-directory bookkeeping as if the deletion had succeeded, orphaning VM 111 on the Proxmox broker host. `gotest.json` shows `TestContainerdCPUs` following the identical sequence at 23:23:52–23:24:15: it builds a fresh `sdn-4bf7e75d` image successfully, then the broker rejects provisioning with `device \"sdn-4bf7e75d\" already exists` and removes its own image directory as cleanup. Live checks confirm the pattern continues — `evetest status` shows \"No EVE devices found\" and `evetest sdn status` reports \"SDN client is not initialized\" (this test's own failure-path teardown ran cleanly locally), but the orphaned VM 111 itself has never been removed on Proxmox. Per `live-ledger.md`, this exact \"VM deletion timeout → stale device blocks same-named recreation\" signature has no occurrence in past nightly runs, so it's a new manifestation (first seen tonight at 23:11:40) of the broader known class of Proxmox broker/VM-lifecycle flakiness, not a previously-documented recurring issue — and it will keep failing every remaining test in the suite until VM 111 is manually cleared on the Proxmox broker host.","time":{"start":1795212602000,"stop":1795212651930,"duration":49930}},{"uid":"9518f0075757ff06","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/27/#testresult/9518f0075757ff06","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795131965000,"stop":1795132170040,"duration":205040}},{"uid":"9fbcfba2ab11cc79","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/25/#testresult/9fbcfba2ab11cc79","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795039947000,"stop":1795040243330,"duration":296330}},{"uid":"ab0dbf332df8d9c8","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/23/#testresult/ab0dbf332df8d9c8","status":"passed","time":{"start":17949531